  "verdict": "SPLIT VERDICT -- LOCATED IN MASS, ABSTAIN IN XI. The wall is cleanly located on the control parameter: m* = 0.0001467 (interior, monotone, both L1 endpoints reproduced). It is NOT located in xi: the crossing sits at xi = 3947 = 7.71x the box, where the correlation envelope decays by only 3.2% across the whole fit window (r <= N/4) -- a correlation length fitted from an essentially flat curve is not a measurement. xi*/N = 7.71 is therefore reported as an UPPER BOUND on nothing useful, not a location. THE PHYSICAL CONTENT: R_CoV leaves the critical baseline while xi is still far OUTSIDE the box, so at this gate's wall the condition xi << N is violated -- E2's boundary cannot be expressed as a xi/N ratio on this system at all. The two conditions (l << xi and xi << N) do not merely fail independently here; the second is already broken where the gate fires."
